<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Bank of Ireland details dividend payout.</title>
<headline>Bank of Ireland details dividend payout.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Ireland Group Plc said on Friday 54 percent of its shareholders had opted to take new units of ordinary stock instead of their final cash dividend under the bank's stock alternative scheme.</p>
<p>As a result, the bank reduced the total cash dividend to be paid on Friday by 7.7 million Irish pounds, or 13.5 percent, and created 1.05 million new units of ordinary stock, Bank of Ireland said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
